{"id":"mahabharata-9-004","work":"mahabharata","part":9,"partName":"शल्यपर्व","partNameEn":"Shalya Parva","unit":4,"title":"चतुर्थोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 4 · Kripa advises peace","summary":{"en":"Kripa tells Duryodhana to make peace with the Pandavas while there is still strength left, recalling Pandava mercy and the might of Krishna and Arjuna. Duryodhana, sighing, replies that peace is no longer possible after what has been done.","kn":"ಇನ್ನೂ ಬಲ ಉಳಿದಿರುವಾಗಲೇ ಪಾಂಡವರೊಡನೆ ಸಂಧಿ ಮಾಡಿಕೊಳ್ಳಲು ಕೃಪ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳಿ ಪಾಂಡವರ ಕರುಣೆ, ಕೃಷ್ಣಾರ್ಜುನರ ಶಕ್ತಿಯನ್ನು ನೆನಪಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ನಿಟ್ಟುಸಿರು ಬಿಟ್ಟ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ಆದ ಕೃತ್ಯಗಳ ನಂತರ ಸಂಧಿ ಇನ್ನು ಸಾಧ್ಯವಿಲ್ಲವೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"कृप दुर्योधन से कहते हैं कि अभी बल शेष रहते पाण्डवों से सन्धि कर लो, और पाण्डवों की दया तथा कृष्ण-अर्जुन की शक्ति याद दिलाते हैं। साँस भरकर दुर्योधन कहता है कि जो हो चुका उसके बाद सन्धि सम्भव नहीं।","te":"ఇంకా బలం మిగిలి ఉండగానే పాండవులతో సంధి చేసుకోమని కృపుడు దుర్యోధనునికి చెప్పి పాండవుల దయను, కృష్ణార్జునుల శక్తిని గుర్తు చేస్తాడు. నిట్టూర్చిన దుర్యోధనుడు జరిగిన దాని తరువాత సంధి ఇక సాధ్యం కాదంటాడు.","ta":"இன்னும் வலிமை இருக்கும்போதே பாண்டவருடன் சமாதானம் செய்யும்படி கிருபர் துரியோதனனிடம் கூறி, பாண்டவரின் கருணையையும் கண்ணன் அர்ஜுனனின் ஆற்றலையும் நினைவூட்டுகிறார். பெருமூச்சுடன் துரியோதனன் நடந்தவற்றுக்குப்பின் சமாதானம் இயலாது என்கிறான்.","ml":"ശക്തി ശേഷിക്കുമ്പോൾ തന്നെ പാണ്ഡവരുമായി സന്ധി ചെയ്യണമെന്ന് കൃപർ ദുര്യോധനനോട് പറയുന്നു; പാണ്ഡവരുടെ ദയയും കൃഷ്ണന്റെയും അർജുനന്റെയും ശക്തിയും അദ്ദേഹം ഓർമ്മിപ്പിക്കുന്നു. ചെയ്തതിനുശേഷം സന്ധി ഇനി സാധ്യമല്ലെന്ന് ദുര്യോധനൻ നെടുവീർപ്പിട്ട് മറുപടി പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 9.4; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jun 23 2020","sections":[{"title":"शल्यपर्व","titleEn":"Shalya Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एवमुक्तस्ततो राजा गौतमेन यशस्विना ।\nनिःश्वस्य दीर्घमुष्णं च तूष्णीमासीद्विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed by the renowned Gautama, the king sighed long and hot and was silent, lord of the people."}},{"n":2,"text":"ततो मुहूर्तं स ध्यात्वा धार्तराष्ट्रो महामनाः ।\nकृपं शारद्वतं वाक्यमित्युवाच परंतपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, after reflecting for a moment, the great-minded son of Dhritarashtra, scorcher of foes, spoke these words to Kripa, son of Sharadvat."}},{"n":3,"text":"यत्किंचित्सुहृदा वाच्यं तत्सर्वं श्रावितो ह्यहम् ।\nकृतं च भवता सर्वं प्राणान्संत्यज्य युध्यता ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Whatever a friend should say, you have told me all of it, and you have done everything, fighting with no care for your life.\""}},{"n":4,"text":"गाहमानमनीकानि युध्यमानं महारथैः ।\nपाण्डवैरतितेजोभिर्लोकस्त्वामनुदृष्टवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The world saw you plunging into the ranks and fighting great warriors of the exceedingly fiery Pandavas.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"सुहृदा यदिदं वाच्यं भवता श्रावितो ह्यहम् ।\nन मां प्रीणाति तत्सर्वं मुमूर्षोरिव भेषजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"But this advice that you as a friend have given me does not please me at all, like medicine to a man who wants to die.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"हेतुकारणसंयुक्तं हितं वचनमुत्तमम् ।\nउच्यमानं महाबाहो न मे विप्राग्र्य रोचते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This excellent counsel, beneficial and backed with reasons, does not appeal to me, mighty-armed best of Brahmins.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"राज्याद्विनिकृतोऽस्माभिः कथं सोऽस्मासु विश्वसेत् ।\nअक्षद्यूते च नृपतिर्जितोऽस्माभिर्महाधनः ।\nस कथं मम वाक्यानि श्रद्दध्याद्भूय एव तु ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"We drove the king from his kingdom; how could he trust us? We beat that wealthy king at dice; how could he ever believe my words again?\""}},{"n":8,"text":"तथा दौत्येन संप्राप्तः कृष्णः पार्थहिते रतः ।\nप्रलब्धश्च हृषीकेशस्तच्च कर्म विरोधितम् ।\nस च मे वचनं ब्रह्मन्कथमेवाभिमंस्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Krishna came as envoy, devoted to the Pandavas' good, and we deceived Hrishikesha; that act made him our foe. Brahmin, how could he accept my word?\""}},{"n":9,"text":"विललाप हि यत्कृष्णा सभामध्ये समेयुषी ।\nन तन्मर्षयते कृष्णो न राज्यहरणं तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"What Draupadi cried when she was brought into the middle of the assembly, Krishna cannot forgive, nor the seizing of the kingdom.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"एकप्राणावुभौ कृष्णावन्योन्यं प्रति संहतौ ।\nपुरा यच्छ्रुतमेवासीदद्य पश्यामि तत्प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The two Krishnas, Krishna and Arjuna, have one life between them, bound to each other; what I heard of old, I see today, lord.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"स्वस्रीयं च हतं श्रुत्वा दुःखं स्वपिति केशवः ।\nकृतागसो वयं तस्य स मदर्थं कथं क्षमेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Hearing that his sister's son is slain, Keshava sleeps in sorrow. We are guilty toward him; how could he spare me?\""}},{"n":12,"text":"अभिमन्योर्विनाशेन न शर्म लभतेऽर्जुनः ।\nस कथं मद्धिते यत्नं प्रकरिष्यति याचितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Arjuna finds no peace since Abhimanyu was destroyed; how will he, though begged, make an effort for my good?\""}},{"n":13,"text":"मध्यमः पाण्डवस्तीक्ष्णो भीमसेनो महाबलः ।\nप्रतिज्ञातं च तेनोग्रं स भज्येत न संनमेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The middle Pandava, fierce Bhimasena of great strength, has sworn a terrible vow; he would break rather than bend.\""}},{"n":14,"text":"उभौ तौ बद्धनिस्त्रिंशावुभौ चाबद्धकङ्कटौ ।\nकृतवैरावुभौ वीरौ यमावपि यमोपमौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Both twins have drawn their swords and tied their belts; both heroes have sworn enmity, and they are like Yama himself.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नः शिखण्डी च कृतवैरौ मया सह ।\nतौ कथं मद्धिते यत्नं प्रकुर्यातां द्विजोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Dhrishtadyumna and Shikhandi have made enmity with me; how, best of Brahmins, would they try for my good?\""}},{"n":16,"text":"दुःशासनेन यत्कृष्णा एकवस्त्रा रजस्वला ।\nपरिक्लिष्टा सभामध्ये सर्वलोकस्य पश्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The Pandavas still remember how Duhshasana tormented Draupadi, in one cloth and in her season, before the eyes of all the world,\""}},{"n":17,"text":"तथा विवसनां दीनां स्मरन्त्यद्यापि पाण्डवाः ।\nन निवारयितुं शक्याः संग्रामात्ते परंतपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"and how she stood disrobed and wretched. Those scorchers of foes cannot be held back from the battle.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"यदा च द्रौपदी कृष्णा मद्विनाशाय दुःखिता ।\nउग्रं तेपे तपः कृष्णा भर्तॄणामर्थसिद्धये ।\nस्थण्डिले नित्यदा शेते यावद्वैरस्य यातना ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"And Draupadi, grieving, practiced fierce austerity for my destruction and for her husbands' success; she sleeps every day on bare ground until the vengeance is done.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"निक्षिप्य मानं दर्पं च वासुदेवसहोदरा ।\nकृष्णायाः प्रेष्यवद्भूत्वा शुश्रूषां कुरुते सदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Setting aside pride and haughtiness, the sister of Vasudeva, Subhadra, always serves Draupadi like a servant.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"इति सर्वं समुन्नद्धं न निर्वाति कथंचन ।\nअभिमन्योर्विनाशेन स संधेयः कथं मया ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So all this is risen up and never at all dies down. With Abhimanyu destroyed, how can I make peace with him?\""}},{"n":21,"text":"कथं च नाम भुक्त्वेमां पृथिवीं सागराम्बराम् ।\nपाण्डवानां प्रसादेन भुञ्जीयां राज्यमल्पकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Having enjoyed this earth bounded by the sea, how could I live on a tiny kingdom by the Pandavas' grace?\""}},{"n":22,"text":"उपर्युपरि राज्ञां वै ज्वलितो भास्करो यथा ।\nयुधिष्ठिरं कथं पश्चादनुयास्यामि दासवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I shone like the sun above all kings; how could I follow Yudhishthira like a servant?\""}},{"n":23,"text":"कथं भुक्त्वा स्वयं भोगान्दत्त्वा दायांश्च पुष्कलान् ।\nकृपणं वर्तयिष्यामि कृपणैः सह जीविकाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Having enjoyed pleasures myself and given ample gifts, how could I make a wretched living among the wretched?\""}},{"n":24,"text":"नाभ्यसूयामि ते वाक्यमुक्तं स्निग्धं हितं त्वया ।\nन तु संधिमहं मन्ये प्राप्तकालं कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I do not scorn your words, which were kind and meant well; but I do not think this is in any way the time for peace.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"सुनीतमनुपश्यामि सुयुद्धेन परंतप ।\nनायं क्लीबयितुं कालः संयोद्धुं काल एव नः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I see good policy only in a good fight, scorcher of foes. This is not the time to turn unmanly; it is the time to fight.\""}},{"n":26,"text":"इष्टं मे बहुभिर्यज्ञैर्दत्ता विप्रेषु दक्षिणाः ।\nप्राप्ताः क्रमश्रुता वेदाः शत्रूणां मूर्ध्नि च स्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I have performed many sacrifices, given fees to Brahmins, studied the Vedas in due order, and planted my foot on my enemies' heads.\""}},{"n":27,"text":"भृत्या मे सुभृतास्तात दीनश्चाभ्युद्धृतो जनः ।\nयातानि परराष्ट्राणि स्वराष्ट्रमनुपालितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I have supported my servants well, raised up the wretched, marched on foreign realms and protected my own.\""}},{"n":28,"text":"भुक्ताश्च विविधा भोगास्त्रिवर्गः सेवितो मया ।\nपितॄणां गतमानृण्यं क्षत्रधर्मस्य चोभयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I have enjoyed varied pleasures and followed the three aims of life; I have paid my debt to my ancestors and to the duty of a Kshatriya.\""}},{"n":29,"text":"न ध्रुवं सुखमस्तीह कुतो राज्यं कुतो यशः ।\nइह कीर्तिर्विधातव्या सा च युद्धेन नान्यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"There is no lasting happiness here, so what of kingdom or fame? Fame must be won here, and it comes through war and not otherwise.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"गृहे यत्क्षत्रियस्यापि निधनं तद्विगर्हितम् ।\nअधर्मः सुमहानेष यच्छय्यामरणं गृहे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Even for a Kshatriya, death at home is blamed; dying in bed at home is a very great wrong.\""}},{"n":31,"text":"अरण्ये यो विमुञ्चेत संग्रामे वा तनुं नरः ।\nक्रतूनाहृत्य महतो महिमानं स गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"A man who gives up his body in the forest or in battle, having performed great sacrifices, attains greatness.\""}},{"n":32,"text":"कृपणं विलपन्नार्तो जरयाभिपरिप्लुतः ।\nम्रियते रुदतां मध्ये ज्ञातीनां न स पूरुषः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"One who dies lamenting pitifully, in distress and overcome by age, amid weeping kinsmen, is not a real man.\""}},{"n":33,"text":"त्यक्त्वा तु विविधान्भोगान्प्राप्तानां परमां गतिम् ।\nअपीदानीं सुयुद्धेन गच्छेयं सत्सलोकताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Giving up many kinds of pleasure, I may now by a good fight go to the world of the good, the supreme goal of those who reach it.\""}},{"n":34,"text":"शूराणामार्यवृत्तानां संग्रामेष्वनिवर्तिनाम् ।\nधीमतां सत्यसंधानां सर्वेषां क्रतुयाजिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"For heroes of noble conduct who never turn back from battles, wise, true to their word, all performers of sacrifices,\""}},{"n":35,"text":"शस्त्रावभृथमाप्तानां ध्रुवं वासस्त्रिविष्टपे ।\nमुदा नूनं प्रपश्यन्ति शुभ्रा ह्यप्सरसां गणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"who have attained the final bath of battle with weapons, a dwelling in heaven is sure; surely the radiant hosts of nymphs look on them gladly.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"पश्यन्ति नूनं पितरः पूजिताञ्शक्रसंसदि ।\nअप्सरोभिः परिवृतान्मोदमानांस्त्रिविष्टपे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Surely their ancestors see them honored in Indra's court, surrounded by nymphs and rejoicing in heaven.\""}},{"n":37,"text":"पन्थानममरैर्यातं शूरैश्चैवानिवर्तिभिः ।\nअपि तैः संगतं मार्गं वयमप्यारुहेमहि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"We too would climb the path that the immortals and heroes who never retreat have trodden, joining those on it,\""}},{"n":38,"text":"पितामहेन वृद्धेन तथाचार्येण धीमता ।\nजयद्रथेन कर्णेन तथा दुःशासनेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"with my old grandfather, the wise teacher, Jayadratha, Karna and Duhshasana.\""}},{"n":39,"text":"घटमाना मदर्थेऽस्मिन्हताः शूरा जनाधिपाः ।\nशेरते लोहिताक्ताङ्गाः पृथिव्यां शरविक्षताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Heroic kings who fought for my sake lie on the earth, their limbs smeared with blood, wounded by arrows.\""}},{"n":40,"text":"उत्तमास्त्रविदः शूरा यथोक्तक्रतुयाजिनः ।\nत्यक्त्वा प्राणान्यथान्यायमिन्द्रसद्मसु धिष्ठिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Heroes who knew the best weapons and sacrificed as prescribed gave up their lives lawfully and are established in Indra's halls.\""}},{"n":41,"text":"तैस्त्वयं रचितः पन्था दुर्गमो हि पुनर्भवेत् ।\nसंपतद्भिर्महावेगैरितो याद्भिश्च सद्गतिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"They have built that path, which would be hard to travel again for those rushing there with great speed on the way to a good end.\""}},{"n":42,"text":"ये मदर्थे हताः शूरास्तेषां कृतमनुस्मरन् ।\nऋणं तत्प्रतिमुञ्चानो न राज्ये मन आदधे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Remembering what those heroes slain for my sake did, and repaying that debt, I have no mind for the kingdom.\""}},{"n":43,"text":"पातयित्वा वयस्यांश्च भ्रातॄनथ पितामहान् ।\nजीवितं यदि रक्षेयं लोको मां गर्हयेद्ध्रुवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If I were to save my own life after getting my friends, brothers and grandfathers killed, the world would surely condemn me.\""}},{"n":44,"text":"कीदृशं च भवेद्राज्यं मम हीनस्य बन्धुभिः ।\nसखिभिश्च सुहृद्भिश्च प्रणिपत्य च पाण्डवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"What would a kingdom be to me, bereft of kinsmen, friends and companions, and having bowed to the Pandava?\""}},{"n":45,"text":"सोऽहमेतादृशं कृत्वा जगतोऽस्य पराभवम् ।\nसुयुद्धेन ततः स्वर्गं प्राप्स्यामि न तदन्यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So having brought about such a defeat of this world, I shall win heaven by a good fight, and not otherwise.\""}},{"n":46,"text":"एवं दुर्योधनेनोक्तं सर्वे संपूज्य तद्वचः ।\nसाधु साध्विति राजानं क्षत्रियाः संबभाषिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Duryodhana had spoken thus, all the Kshatriyas honored his words and said to the king, \"Well said, well said.\""}},{"n":47,"text":"पराजयमशोचन्तः कृतचित्ताश्च विक्रमे ।\nसर्वे सुनिश्चिता योद्धुमुदग्रमनसोऽभवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Not grieving over defeat, resolved on valor, they were all firmly determined to fight, with spirits high."}},{"n":48,"text":"ततो वाहान्समाश्वास्य सर्वे युद्धाभिनन्दिनः ।\nऊने द्वियोजने गत्वा प्रत्यतिष्ठन्त कौरवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, refreshing their mounts, all the Kauravas, delighting in battle, went a little less than two yojanas and halted."}},{"n":49,"text":"आकाशे विद्रुमे पुण्ये प्रस्थे हिमवतः शुभे ।\nअरुणां सरस्वतीं प्राप्य पपुः सस्नुश्च तज्जलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, on a holy, auspicious Himalayan slope, they reached the red Sarasvati, drank its water and bathed in it."}},{"n":50,"text":"तव पुत्राः कृतोत्साहाः पर्यवर्तन्त ते ततः ।\nपर्यवस्थाप्य चात्मानमन्योन्येन पुनस्तदा ।\nसर्वे राजन्न्यवर्तन्त क्षत्रियाः कालचोदिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your sons, with their courage raised, then turned back; having steadied themselves among each other again, all the Kshatriyas returned, king, driven by Time."}}]}]}